# ThinkPad X12: let PCI devices runtime-suspend when idle (the default leaves about a dozen
# chipset devices always on). Measured at settled idle: about 0.1-0.15 W less.
ACTION=="add|bind", SUBSYSTEM=="pci", ATTR{power/control}="auto"
# Keep the LTE modem on "on". A modem with no driver bound (iosm failed to start it, or iosm
# not loaded) runtime-suspends on "auto", its root port follows, the firmware's RTD3 holds the
# card in reset, and the system hangs (garbled screen, CPU spinning) a few seconds into boot.
# With the stock iosm driver, "auto" also hangs hibernation (docs/07-lte-modem-gps.md).
ACTION=="add|bind", SUBSYSTEM=="pci", ATTR{vendor}=="0x8086", ATTR{device}=="0x7360", ATTR{power/control}="on"
